Subject SHA-256 3962928d6d8238f8c521b06e5d4f6dfa4e4b4f26aef2ce72d7ce96674a0a4393:
  target/frontend/release/evocc --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu --emit=asm full-memory-barrier.c
  gcc-14 -no-pie full-memory-barrier.s -o /tmp/barrier
  /tmp/barrier
Native exit 0; publish: str w0 (data), dmb ish, str w1 (ready).
C-HIR and EvoIR interpreters reach E3021, as the ordered-assembly boundary requires.

The native exits check values and the void/unevaluated type query. They do not
by themselves establish inter-thread ordering: that requirement is checked by
the emitted full-barrier instruction and ordered memory-clobber representation.
